ber}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/deployments","created_at":"2023-08-05T07:56:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T06:52:14Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-18T05:40:12Z","git_url":"git://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:MohamedRejeb/Calf.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/MohamedRejeb/Calf","homepage":"https://mohamedrejeb.github.io/Calf/","size":12888,"stargazers_count":1748,"watchers_count":1748,"language":"Kotlin","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":93,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":17,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["android","compose","compose-desktop","compose-ios","compose-library","compose-multiplatform","compose-multiplatform-library","compose-ui","desktop","ios","jetpack-compose","kotlin","kotlin-multiplatform"],"visibility":"public","forks":93,"open_issues":17,"watchers":1748,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Motivation\n\nI have an import data button. Data is usually in a zip format. The file can be bit and I don't want to load it in memory. \n\nHowever, on Android I have to. I can't use `KmpFile.getPath()` and then use a library like https://github.com/henrik242/kmp-zip to read it as a stream via for instance their okio module. The problem is that often times especially when selecting from Google Drive or the Downloads you get a `Uri` back and you need to use `activity.contentResolver.openInputStream`. What's even worse is that even when Android gives me a `Uri`, `kmpFile.isFile(context)` returns true. \n\nFirst step: Fix `kmpFile.isFile(context)` to return false on Android if it's a uri.\n\n\n### Proposed Solution\n\nSecond: Provide some kind of API such that I can read the selected file as a stream.\n\nThis is my current code:\n\n```kotlin\nval canImportFile = when (platform()) {\n  Platform.ANDROID -> false // Uris are not files!\n  Platform.IOS -> true\n  Platform.DESKTOP -> true\n}\n\nreturn when {\n  canImportFile && kmpFile.isFile(context) -> kmpFile.getPath(context)\n    ?.toPath()\n    ?.let { path -> ZipInputStream(FileSystem.SYSTEM.source(path).buffer()) }\n  else -> null\n} ?: ZipInputStream(kmpFile.readByteArray(context))\n```\n\nFor the second proposal I think the best solution would be to have a new module `calf-file-picker-okio` that just has an extension function like `kmpFile.source(context)` which returns me an okio `Source`. Android uses the `contentResolver.openInputStream().source()` extension method and just returns it. On the other platforms you could just do what I'm doing with the `FileSystem.SYSTEM.source()` call.\n\n### Module\n\ncalf-file-picker\n\n### Specify Other Module (if you selected \"other\" above)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Target Platform(s)\n\nAndroid","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/issues/537/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MohamedRejeb/Calf/issues/537/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]